# CRONTAB.SAMPLE - crontab for the news user (crontab -u news crontab.sample)
#
# The scripts are installed to <path_home>/adm (default /news/adm) by
# "make install".  They find their programs and paths themselves (dbin next
# to adm, paths through dpath), so the news user's home directory doesn't
# matter.  Adjust /news below if you installed with another PREFIX, and the
# log directory if path_log isn't /news/log (see "dbin/dpath log").
#
# NOTE - some crons don't understand the */nn format; list the minutes
#	 instead, e.g. 0,5,10,15,20,25,30,35,40,45,50,55.
#
# Every 5 minutes: flush the outgoing queues and start the dnewslink workers.
*/5 * * * *	/news/dbin/dspoolout >> /news/log/dspoolout.log 2>&1
#
# Every hour: expire the spool (skipped while a history trim holds the lock).
50 * * * *	/news/adm/hourly.expire >> /news/log/daily.log 2>&1
#
# Daily: rotate the logs.
40 2 * * *	/news/adm/daily.atrim >> /news/log/daily.log 2>&1
#
# Twice a week: trim the history file (dhisexpire) and the active file.
30 2 * * 1,4	/news/adm/biweekly.atrim >> /news/log/daily.log 2>&1
#
# Reader (dreaderd) machines only: expire the overview and the article cache
# daily, rewrite the overview data weekly.
#45 2 * * *	/news/adm/daily.reader >> /news/log/daily.log 2>&1
#30 3 * * 0	/news/adm/weekly.reader >> /news/log/daily.log 2>&1
